# LeakSanitizer suppressions for scripts/leak-check.sh.
#
# Each line hides every leak whose allocation stack passes a matching frame, any
# depth. Broad entry (whole library, anything event loop calls) hides our leaks
# too (shim runs under Qt event loop). Only functions never calling back into
# our code, each with reason.
#
# From piirit's, measured on same Qt 5.15 (Ubuntu) across its suite; kept only
# while vuo's run needs them.

# Offscreen platform plugin creates QScreen, QPlatformScreen, cursor at startup,
# never deletes; mutual pointers → LeakSanitizer sees unreachable cycle. Qt's
# own, once per process, offscreen platform only.
leak:QGuiApplicationPrivate::createPlatformIntegration

# QML connections to same screen (`Screen` attached property, window watching
# its screen) live in leaked screen's connection list, reported with it.
leak:QQuickScreenInfo::setWrappedScreen
leak:QQuickWindowPrivate::init
